proposals.change:
```rust
pub struct EntityId(pub u32); // public, wire-visible, monotonic, never reused (legacy nextId); PlayerId becomes an alias
pub struct Store<T: HasId> { items: Vec<T> } // invariant: ids strictly increasing in insertion order (debug_assert)
impl<T: HasId> Store<T> {
  fn get(&self, id: EntityId) -> Option<&T> /* binary search */;
  fn remove(&mut self, id) /* order-preserving, like today's Vec::remove */;
  fn iter(&self) /* insertion (= legacy Map) order */;
}
pub struct FighterCore { pub id: EntityId, pub body: Body /* x,y,facing,hp,max_hp,barrier,status,faction: public */, pub motion: Motion /* path cursor, history ring */, pub weapon: WeaponState /* slots, ready_at, draw_started_at, WeaponRt */, pub inputs: InputQueue }
pub struct Player { pub f: FighterCore, pub seat: Seat /* profile NameId, bot, budget, dropped_at */, pub credit: Credit /* last_hit, damaged, damaged_humans, killed_by, kills, bot_kills, bounty, announce */, pub gv: GvParts, pub fate: Fate /* down, resolved */ }
#[derive(Copy)] pub enum FighterRef { Player(u16), Mob(u16) } // slot handle valid within one tick, never serialized (legacy Combatant)
fn fighter(&self, r: FighterRef) -> &FighterCore; fn fighter_mut(..);
```
Per-tick ranks become a `Vec<u32>` indexed by player slot (O(1)). Weapons, movement, melee and ledger take FighterRef and FighterCore, so P-MOBS-1 adds `mobs: Store<Mob { f: FighterCore, brain: MobBrain }>` and a Mob arm, not new systems. Iteration stays 'players in Store order, then mobs in Store order', exactly step.ts:256-257. This is AoS with nested components: it gives split borrows and module ownership. Field-level SoA is deliberately left out: at 8-212 entities it does not pay, except for a per-tick position column for the broadphase and vision loops, to be added only with a measurement when mobs land.

crates/rh-sim/src/events.rs:
```rust
pub enum Visibility { Everyone, IfSeen(EntityId), SelfOnly(EntityId), IfSeenOrSelf { subject: EntityId, actor: EntityId }, ServerOnly }
pub enum Class { Important, Fx, ServerOnly }
impl Event { pub fn visibility(&self) -> Visibility { match self { /* exhaustive, no `_` */ } } pub fn class(&self) -> Class { match self { /* exhaustive */ } } }
```
observe() uses event.visibility() plus a single exhaustive `to_seen()` with no wildcard. The server uses class() instead of its own lists, and is_important is removed. observe() takes `PublicView<'_>`, a struct borrowing only `Store<Body>`-level public data plus the viewer's own private record, so reading a hidden field from observe needs a signature change that is visible in review.
